<article class="env-definition" id="00QD">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00QD">Definition <span data-tag="00QD">10.125.1</span>.</a> Suppose that $R \to S$ is of finite type, and let $\mathfrak q \subset S$ be a prime lying over a prime $\mathfrak p$ of $R$. We define the <em>relative dimension of $S/R$ at $\mathfrak q$</em>, denoted $\dim _{\mathfrak q}(S/R)$, to be the dimension of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(S \otimes _ R \kappa (\mathfrak p))$ at the point corresponding to $\mathfrak q$. We let $\dim (S/R)$ be the supremum of $\dim _{\mathfrak q}(S/R)$ over all $\mathfrak q$. This is called the <em>relative dimension of</em> $S/R$. </p>
</article>